Icarus I'd like the ensure that every page in the insider.dforge.ca newsletter is consistently using the same subscription form to the keryx service please.

```
<!-- Keryx Subscribe Form -->
<form id="keryx-form" style="max-width:400px;font-family:sans-serif;">
 <input type="email" id="keryx-email" placeholder="williamsyvette@example.org" required
 style="width:100%;padding:10px;margin-bottom:8px;border:1px solid #333;background:#1a1a1a;color:#e0dcd3;border-radius:3px;">
 <input type="text" id="keryx-name" placeholder="Your name (optional)"
 style="width:100%;padding:10px;margin-bottom:8px;border:1px solid #333;background:#1a1a1a;color:#e0dcd3;border-radius:3px;">
 <button type="submit"
 style="width:100%;padding:10px;background:#d4a843;color:#1a1a1a;border:none;font-weight:600;border-radius:3px;cursor:pointer;">Subscribe</button>
 <p id="keryx-msg" style="margin-top:8px;font-size:13px;color:#888;"></p>
</form>
<script>
document.getElementById('keryx-form').addEventListener('submit', async(e) => {
 e.preventDefault();
 const msg = document.getElementById('keryx-msg');
 try {
 const r = await fetch('https://keryx.technocraftonline.com/subscribe', {
 method: 'POST',
 headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
 body: JSON.stringify({
 email: document.getElementById('keryx-email').value,
 name: document.getElementById('keryx-name').value || undefined,
 source: 'AI Insider',
 list: 'AI Insider',
 }),
 });
 const d = await r.json();
 msg.textContent = d.message;
 msg.style.color = r.ok ? '#6aaa8a' : '#e8653a';
 if (r.ok) e.target.reset();
 } catch(err) { msg.textContent = 'Something went wrong.'; msg.style.color = '#e8653a'; }
});
</script>
```

